<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA rice export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 21,400 MT were down 70 percent from the week earlier and 45 percent from the 4-week average.</p>
<p>Colombia (8,500 MT--all rough) was the primary buyer, with smaller quantities to Nicaragua (4,200 MT), Mexico (4,200 MT, of which 3,100 MT was rough), the Netherlands (2,100 MT), and Belgium (1,300 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 31,500 MT were 16 percent below the week earlier and 29 percent under the 4-week average.  The major destinations were Saudi Arabia (19,500 MT), Colombia (5,000 MT), and Mexico (4,100 MT).</p>
</text>
